      "problem": "Which of the following matrices has a rank of $4?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that a matrix of rank $4$ must have at least $4$ columns and at least $4$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the following matrices:\n\n- $B$ since it has only $3$ rows.\n\n- $D$ since it has only $3$ columns (and only $3$ rows).\n\n- $E$ since it has only $3$ coumns.\n\nAlso, the matrix must have $4$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $C$ has exactly $4$ pivot columns, while the matrix $A$ has only $2$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(C)=4$ and $\\text{rank}(A)=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the matrix $C.$",
